n96:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n97:    \"\"\"Recolor each framed interior mask with the color from the next red frame clockwise around the blue connector cycle.\n111:    \"\"\"\n168:    \"\"\"Generate an 8-connected mask for frame interior with fill 30-56%.\"\"\"\n203:    \"\"\"Return an inclusive straight segment between row- or column-aligned cells.\"\"\"\n246:    \"\"\"Find an L-shaped path (0-2 turns) from start to end avoiding occupied cells.\"\"\"\n278:    \"\"\"Pick an attachment point on the given side of a frame border.\n317:    \"\"\"Determine which side of a frame is closest to a target point.\"\"\"\n358:    \"\"\"Place non-overlapping frame boxes in clockwise angular order.\"\"\"\n395:    \"\"\"Return frame indexes sorted by angle around their shared centroid.\"\"\"\n432:    \"\"\"Draw frame borders and colored interior masks; return the occupied cells.\"\"\"\n456:    \"\"\"Connect adjacent clockwise frames with bounded blue paths.\"\"\"\n522:def generate_input():\nFILE:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/cf5fd0ad.py\n9:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n10:    \"\"\"Build a four-quadrant rotational tiling of the input square.\n22:    \"\"\"\n79:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
