{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '51,110p;251,360p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8a6d367c.py\"","aggregated_output":"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Complete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n    - The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n    - The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n\n    Rule:\n    - Crop to the rectangular frame.\n    - Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n    - Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n\n    Key insight:\n    The lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\n    frame_color, (r0, c0, r1, c1) = _find_frame(g, bg)\n\n    out = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1].copy()\n    interior = out[1:-1, 1:-1]\n    fill_colors = set(map(int, np.unique(interior))) - {bg, frame_color}\n    assert len(fill_colors) == 1, \"frame interior must contain exactly one fill color\"\n    fill_color = fill_colors.pop()\n\n    seed = interior == fill_color\n    assert np.any(seed), \"frame must contain seed pixels\"\n    ih, iw = seed.shape\n\n    matches: list[np.ndarray] = []\n    for template in _templates_above_frame(g, bg, r0):\n        th, tw = template.shape\n        if ih % th != 0 or iw % tw != 0:\n            continue\n        scale_h = ih // th\n        scale_w = iw // tw\n        if scale_h != scale_w:\n            continue\n\n        scaled = np.kron(template, np.ones((scale_h, scale_w), dtype=bool))\n        if np.all(~seed | scaled):\n            matches.append(scaled)\n\n    assert len(matches) == 1, \"seed pixels must select exactly one scaled template\"\n    completed = matches[0]\n    assert completed.shape == interior.shape\n\n    interior[:, :] = bg\n    interior[completed] = fill_color\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (att2) ---------------\n\nGEN_BG = 8\nGEN_GRID_SHAPE = (27, 21)\nGEN_TEMPLATE_SHAPES = [(3, 3), (3, 4), (4, 3)]\nGEN_TEMPLATE_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 6)\nGEN_TEMPLATE_ROW = 1\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    for _ in range(GEN_ATTEMPTS):\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\n        if grid is not None:\n            return grid\n    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate valid 8a6d367c input\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '282,340p;700,820p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py\"","aggregated_output":"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.\n    - Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.\n    - Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.\n    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.\n\n    Rule:\n    - For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.\n    - The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.\n    - For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.\n    - All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.\n    - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.\n\n    Key insight:\n    - The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    out = _solve_unrotated(g)\n    l9 = _find_l9_orientation(g)\n    if l9 == 'top_right':\n        return np.rot90(out, 1)\n    if l9 == 'top_left':\n        return np.rot90(out, 3)\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (l9rot) ---------------\n\n# ── Tunable constants ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Canvas / region sizing\nGRID_SIZE_MAX = 30                          # max rows or cols\nMIN_REGION_CELLS = 6                        # per-spec minimum\nREGION_SIZE_FACTOR = 2.5                    # min_grid_dim = max(9, n_regions * this)\nREGION_COUNTS = [4, 5, 6, 7, 8]            # candidate region counts\nREGION_WEIGHTS = [3, 3, 3, 1, 1]           # sampling weights for REGION_COUNTS\n\n# Marker counts (spec: 4-8 total, 2-6 normal, 0-2 colored)\nMARKER_MIN = 4\nMARKER_MAX = 8\nNORMAL_MAX = 6\nCOLORED_MAX = 2\n\n# Color pool (all ARC colors except 1, which is reserved for T-marker cells)\nCOLOR_POOL = [c for c in range(10) if c != 1]\n\n# L9 rotation marker\nL9_PROBABILITY = 0.5                        # chance of placing a rotation marker\nL9_OFFSETS = {                              # 5-cell L offsets keyed by corner orientation\n    'top_right': [(0, 0), (0, -1), (0, -2), (1, 0), (2, 0)],\n    'top_left':  [(0, 0), (0,  1), (0,  2), (1, 0), (2, 0)],\n}\n\n# Generation retry budget\nSEED_ATTEMPTS = 200                         # tries to place n distinct region seeds\nGEN_RETRIES = 300                           # outer generate_input retry budget\n\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    for _ in range(GEN_RETRIES):\n        result = _gen_attempt()\n        if result is not None:\n            return result\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Failed to generate valid input after {GEN_RETRIES} attempts\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
